    "semantic_notes": [
      {
        "heading": "[ edit L6a3 Quick Notes ]",
        "text": "The link L6a3 is [math]\\displaystyle{ 6^2_1 }[/math] in the Rolfsen table of links. It is often seen in \"Magen David\" (star of David) necklaces. [ edit L6a3 Further Notes and Views ] Ruberman, Cochran, Melvin, Akbulut, Gompf, Kirby [1] Rich Schwartz' \"72\" [2] Triangle interlaced with a circle, a traditional symbol of the Christian Trinity (less used in recent centuries) An architectural trefoil (the outline of three overlapping circles) interlaced with an equilateral triangle, another old Christian Trinitarian symbol. Closed granny knot. Further images Celtic flag proposal. Flag of Blonay, Vaud, Switzerland. \"Eye of Providence\" inside triangle interlaced with circle, Venice.",
        "source": "rendered-text-window"
      },
      {
        "heading": "[ edit L6a3 Further Notes and Views ]",
        "text": "Ruberman, Cochran, Melvin, Akbulut, Gompf, Kirby [1] Rich Schwartz' \"72\" [2] Triangle interlaced with a circle, a traditional symbol of the Christian Trinity (less used in recent centuries) An architectural trefoil (the outline of three overlapping circles) interlaced with an equilateral triangle, another old Christian Trinitarian symbol. Closed granny knot. Further images Celtic flag proposal. Flag of Blonay, Vaud, Switzerland. \"Eye of Providence\" inside triangle interlaced with circle, Venice. Composed of intersecting circles. Hindu hexagram symbol with Aum/Om, from Nepal.",
        "source": "rendered-text-window"
      }
    ],
